---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import camps from '../data/tribe_camps.json';

// Mechanic transcribed from Tile.doTurn → skipImprovementUnitTurns /
// resetImprovementUnitTurns / countTribeAvailableUnits (reference/Source —
// all drift-watched in verify_source_constants.py). Patch 1.0.84658 removed
// the old kill acceleration from Unit.makeDead; see tribe_camps.json
// code.killAccelRemovedIn. XML-derived numbers
// (tribe_camps.json, build_tribes.py): settlement tiers from improvement.xml,
// per-Tribal-Level knobs from tribeLevel.xml.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const range = camps.levels[0]?.maxUnitsRange ?? 3;
---

<Base
  title="Camp Unit Spawning"
  active="camp-spawning"
  pageMark="🏕️"
  description={`When tribal camps in Old World spawn units and when they do not. Covers the spawn countdown, which is ${camps.baseUnitTurns} turns at base and ${camps.levels.map((l: any) => l.interval).join(', ')} turns by the Tribal Strength setting, the pause rule that freezes a full camp's countdown, and the develop timer that upgrades the camp's tier. Transcribed from Tile.cs in the game source. Patch ${camps.code.killAccelRemovedIn} removed the old kill acceleration.`}
  pageStats={[
    { label: 'base interval', value: `${camps.baseUnitTurns}t` },
    { label: 'camp tiers', value: camps.settlements.length },
    { label: 'count radius', value: `${range} tiles` },
  ]}
>
  <p class="lede">
    Every tribal settlement runs a <b>spawn countdown</b>. The countdown falls
    each turn <em>only while the camp is not already full</em>, and when it
    reaches zero a unit appears and the countdown resets. The only way to slow a
    camp down is to keep its garrison at the cap, which freezes the timer. The
    rules come from <code>Tile.skipImprovementUnitTurns</code> and
    <code>resetImprovementUnitTurns</code> in the game source, and the numbers
    come from <code>improvement.xml</code> and <code>tribeLevel.xml</code>.
  </p>

  <section class="cs-section">
    <h2 class="cs-h2">The pause rule</h2>
    <div class="cs-rule">
      A camp is full, and its countdown is <em>frozen</em>, while the tribe's
      units within <b>{range} tiles</b> reach the cap. Units that are out raiding
      do not count.
      <div class="cs-formula">cap = camp tier (+1 to +4) + Tribal Strength bonus (+0 to +4)</div>
      <ul class="cs-rule__mods">
        <li><b>Camp tier</b> is the settlement's level, from Hovel at +1 up to Bastion at +4, as listed in the table below.</li>
        <li><b>Tribal Strength</b> is the option in advanced setup, running from Passive to Raging, and called Tribal Level in the game files. Each step adds a flat bonus to every camp's cap, from Passive +0 through Weak +1, Normal +2 and Strong +3 to Raging +4, and it also shortens the spawn interval.</li>
        <li>The cap is <b>halved</b>, rounded up, when no city the tribe could raid is within its raid range.</li>
        <li>The cap is never more than a third of the tiles on the landmass, so a small island caps low.</li>
      </ul>
      Killing a unit near a full camp no longer shortens the timer, because patch
      {camps.code.killAccelRemovedIn} removed that. What a kill does is drop the
      garrison below the cap, which restarts the countdown.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-section">
    <h2 class="cs-h2">Reading the two timers on a camp</h2>
    <p class="cs-body">
      A camp shows two counters. The first is the <b>next unit timer</b>, and
      below it is the <b>develop timer</b>, which is the time until the camp
      upgrades to its next tier. In the code only three things move the next unit
      timer. It falls by <b>1</b> per turn while running, and the tile tooltip adds
      <em>"(PAUSED)"</em> while the camp sits at its cap. It gains <b>2</b> turns
      when the camp develops, and it <b>resets to full</b> when a unit spawns.
      Since patch {camps.code.killAccelRemovedIn}, unit deaths do not move it.
    </p>
    <ul class="cs-notes">
      <li>
        <b>The develop timer</b> counts up toward the tier's threshold, and each
        camp also rolls a random head start of up to 10 turns when it is placed,
        scaled down at lower Tribal Strength settings. The timer <b>pauses while a
        foreign unit stands on the camp tile</b>. When the camp upgrades it starts
        rolling the stronger tier's units, and its next unit timer gains 2 turns.
      </li>
      <li>
        Movement changes the freeze as often as combat does, whether raiders
        leave or return, units cross the ring of {range} tiles, or a nearby city
        becomes raidable, which doubles the cap.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-section">
    <h2 class="cs-h2">The numbers</h2>
    <div class="cs-cols">
      <div>
        <h3 class="cs-sub">By Tribal Strength, the advanced setup option</h3>
        <table class="cs-tbl">
          <thead><tr><th>Tribal Strength</th><th>New unit every</th><th>Camp cap bonus</th><th>Raid range</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {camps.levels.map((l: any) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{l.name}</td>
                <td><b>{l.interval}</b> turns</td>
                <td>+{l.defendUnits}</td>
                <td>{l.raidRange > 0 ? `${l.raidRange} tiles` : '—'}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="cs-sub">By camp tier, which settlements reach over time</h3>
        <table class="cs-tbl">
          <thead><tr><th>Camp</th><th>Camp cap base</th><th>Develops in</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {camps.settlements.map((s: any) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{s.name}</td>
                <td>+{s.defendUnits}</td>
                <td>{s.developTurns > 0 ? `${s.developTurns} turns` : 'top tier'}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cs-note">
      For example, at Normal an Outpost caps at 2 + 2, which is <b>4</b> units
      within {range} tiles, or <b>2</b> when it has no city to raid in range.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="cs-section">
    <h2 class="cs-h2">What follows from the rules</h2>
    <ul class="cs-notes">
      <li><b>A camp near your borders keeps producing.</b> With a city it can raid in range, it holds <b>twice the standing force</b> before it pauses.</li>
      <li><b>Raiders do not count.</b> Units that leave to raid stop counting against the cap, so a camp keeps spawning while its warband is away.</li>
      <li><b>Standing on a camp stops its upgrade</b>, because the develop timer does not run while a foreign unit occupies the camp tile. Occupation does not affect the next unit timer, which only the cap governs.</li>
      <li>The very first countdown of the game is <b>halved on turn 1</b>.</li>
      <li>In co-op multiplayer, where every player is on one team, intervals scale by 4/(3+players), so more players mean faster camps.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="provenance">
The mechanic is transcribed from <code>Tile.doTurn</code>, which calls
    <code>skipImprovementUnitTurns</code>, <code>resetImprovementUnitTurns</code>
    and <code>countTribeAvailableUnits</code> in the game source. Intervals, camp
    tiers and the Tribal Level settings are read from the game's XML each patch.
    This site hashes those source functions, so a patch that changes the pause
    rule raises an alarm here. See also
    <a href={`${base}tribes`}>Tribes</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-soft);
    max-width: 70ch; margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .lede b { color: var(--text); }
  .lede code, .cs-rule code, .provenance code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-style: normal; font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .cs-section { margin-bottom: 1.8rem; }
  .cs-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold-deep); padding-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }
  .cs-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 0.62rem; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--gold-soft); font-weight: 500; margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }

  .cs-rule {
    font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text-soft); max-width: 76ch;
    background: var(--bg-elev); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold-deep); border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  }
  .cs-rule b { color: var(--text); }
  .cs-formula {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--gold-soft);
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25); border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem; margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .cs-rule__mods { margin: 0.2rem 0 0.6rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .cs-rule__mods li { margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }

  .cs-cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(19rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.2rem; }
  .cs-tbl { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.84rem; }
  .cs-tbl th {
    font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 0.6rem; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--text-faint); text-align: left;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem 0.25rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .cs-tbl td { padding: 0.3rem 0.7rem 0.3rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--border) 55%, transparent); color: var(--text-soft); }
  .cs-tbl td b { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--text); }
  .cs-note { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-dim); margin: 0.6rem 0 0; }
  .cs-note b { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--gold-soft); }

  .cs-body { font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-soft); max-width: 74ch; margin: 0.3rem 0 0.6rem; }
  .cs-body b { color: var(--text); }
  .cs-notes { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; max-width: 76ch; }
  .cs-notes li { font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-soft); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .cs-notes b { color: var(--text); }

  .provenance { margin: 1.6rem 0 0; font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--text-faint); line-height: 1.55; max-width: 80ch; }
  .provenance a { color: var(--gold-soft); }
</style>
